From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:30:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bound disk spill in threaded SQLite databases

Charge the WAL frame extent of an active SQL transaction and the logical
extent of live SQLite temporary files to both the database and durable
process. Release WAL charges after settlement and temporary-file charges
on truncation and close.

Preserve committed frames during rollback cleanup. Open guarded temporary
files through the durable directory capability and close each guarded
connection synchronously before its VFS or budget is destroyed.

